# .scrub-glossary — organization/project-specific terms to scrub before commit.
#
# Copy this file to the repository root as `.scrub-glossary`.
# One term per line. Matching is case-insensitive and literal (not regex).
#
# Two forms are supported:
#   TERM                  -> flagged for review, no suggested replacement
#   TERM => REPLACEMENT    -> flagged with a suggested replacement string
#
# Lines starting with # are comments. Blank lines are ignored.
#
# Register here every name that must NOT leak into shared artifacts:
#   - client / customer names
#   - internal project / product codenames
#   - team, department, or org-internal system names
#   - internal hostnames, repo names, ticket prefixes
#
# NOTE: a glossary only catches terms you have registered. Unregistered terms
# are caught (best-effort) by Claude's LLM review, not by this file. Keep it
# updated as new names appear.

# --- Examples (delete these and add your own) ---
Acme Corporation => SampleCompany
Project Bluebird => ProjectX
internal-jenkins.acme.local => ci.example.com
ACME-  => TICKET-
